## Summary
The article reports that one-third of individuals rushed to emergency rooms due to addiction are in their teens or twenties. This number has doubled over the past decade, indicating a growing crisis of addiction among young people.

## Key Points
- One out of every three addiction-related emergency visits involves individuals aged 10-29.
- The frequency of such visits has doubled in the last ten years.
- This trend highlights a significant public health concern regarding youth addiction.


